Commit: 80bc51e7884d270dacc2c0aeba150079ad4dec36&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="506721" author="adilger" created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:53:26 +0000">&lt;p&gt;This is the cause of recovery-small test_134 failures in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18302" title="recovery-small test_134: FAIL: rm failed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18302"&gt;LU-18302&lt;/a&gt; (22-33% of master failover-part-1 runs in Nov 2026, also failover-zfs-part-1).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the 2026-11-22 failover-part-1 run (test set d9b8fe86), a client's first unlink on MDT0001 after remount was replied with transno 910533066780 and last_committed 0. The HARD failover came about 1s later, so the new client records in last_rcvd were never committed. MDT0000 and MDT0001 then denied all three clients as new during recovery and evicted them, so an acknowledged unlink was lost.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two places lose the th_sync that tgt_last_rcvd_update() sets from exp_need_sync:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;MDT (ldiskfs and ZFS): dt_txn_hook_stop() passes th-&amp;gt;th_top to tgt_txn_stop_cb(), so th_sync is set on the top thandle after top_trans_stop() has copied it to the sub thandle, and osd_trans_stop() only checks the sub thandle. Since c233f39a0159 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-3534" title="async update cross-MDTs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-3534"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-3534&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, v2_7_54_0-42-gc233f39a0159, in 2.7.55).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;osd-zfs: osd_trans_stop() reads th_sync before calling dt_txn_hook_stop(), so every sync set by the hook is ignored. Since 9b704e4088d8 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-5242" title="Test hang sanity test_132, test_133: umount ost" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-5242"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-5242&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, v2_7_53_0-27-g9b704e4088d8, in 2.7.54).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;OFD and OUT are not affected, since they set th_sync from exp_need_sync when the transaction is created.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Verified on an ldiskfs VM with a fail_loc to switch the propagation off:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;off: top th_sync=1, sub th_sync=0, and the first create after mount gets last_committed 0 (3/3)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;on: sub th_sync=1, and last_committed equals the create's transno (3/3)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;replay_barrier_nosync + fail mds1 after the first create: the client is denied as new, evicted, and the file is lost without the fix (2/2); it is kept with the fix (2/2)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/46596" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/46596&lt;/a&gt; is rebased on master as PS8, with the test moved to replay-single test_0e. &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/71308" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/71308&lt;/a&gt; (which synced the MDTs in test_134 instead) is abandoned.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
